<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Wolpert (1969) French Flag positional information, Tickle-Wolpert (1975) chick limb ZPA digit duplication, Ben-Zvi-Barkai (2010) scaling & 2D AER-FGF / ZPA-Shh limb bud paddle (Chick embryo (Gallus gallus domesticus) wing bud & embryonic blastoderm)",
        "Wolpert (1969) French Flag positional information, Tickle-Wolpert (1975) chick limb ZPA digit duplication, Ben-Zvi-Barkai (2010) scaling & 2D AER-FGF / ZPA-Shh limb bud paddle faithfully reproduces Chick embryo (Gallus gallus domesticus) wing bud & embryonic blastoderm morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-8> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Chick embryo (Gallus gallus domesticus) wing bud & embryonic blastoderm specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-french-flag-morphogen-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/469bf3c/1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py> ;
    schema:about "Chick embryo (Gallus gallus domesticus) wing bud & embryonic blastoderm" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Digit condensation or Turing-type periodicity, temporal integration of Shh exposure (Harfe 2004), a dorsoventral axis or 3D geometry, measured growth curves of the chick wing bud, quantitative Fgf4 / Shh expression levels, or a mechanistic derivation of AER and ZPA position",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D linear source-sink and SDD solvers (analytic + explicit PDE, RMSE 7.6e-6), 6-stage growth-scaling sweep with expansion-repression, 5-regime 1D ZPA suite (wild type, full / attenuated / weak anterior graft, ablation) read by a morphogen-valley digit rule, 400-trial Monte Carlo positional-error test, radial segmentation of the vendored 72 h embryo photograph",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: explicit 2D finite-difference solver for FGF and Shh on a growing paddle mask (dx = 12.5 um) with zero-flux boundaries, Michaelis-form Shh<->FGF feedback, AER-driven distal apposition growth, graft dose series, AER excision at five stages, ZPA ablation, a rectangle verification against the 1D cosh steady state, 8 new reference-anchored measurements and 7 new Lean 4 theorems",
        "reported_in_source: Ben-Zvi & Barkai (2010): an expander produced where morphogen is low scales the decay length with domain size",
        "reported_in_source: Laufer et al. (1994) and Niswander et al. (1994): Shh in the ZPA and Fgf4 in the posterior AER maintain each other (Shh lost after AER removal, rescued by FGF4 bead; ectopic anterior Fgf4 after a ZPA graft); Crossley et al. (1996): Fgf8 is expressed along the whole ridge",
        "reported_in_source: Saunders (1948) and Summerbell (1974): AER removal arrests outgrowth and truncates the limb at a level that is progressively more distal the later the excision; Summerbell, Lewis & Wolpert (1973): proximo-distal values are laid down by time spent in the distal progress zone",
        "reported_in_source: Tickle, Summerbell & Wolpert (1975) and Tickle (1981): a posterior ZPA specifies wing digits 2-3-4; an anterior graft gives the mirror duplication 4-3-2-2-3-4, and the digit specified next to a weaker graft advances 2 -> 3 -> 4 with polarizing-cell number; Riddle et al. (1993): Shh mediates ZPA activity",
        "reported_in_source: Wolpert (1969): positional information read from a monotone morphogen gradient against thresholds gives size-invariant French-Flag proportions under linear source-sink diffusion; Crick (1970): synthesis-diffusion-degradation gives lambda = sqrt(D/k) and the positional-error law sigma_x = sigma_c / |dc/dx|",
        "transfer_boundary: Digit identity is read from the instantaneous distal Shh concentration against the Pass 2 thresholds normalised to the wild-type peak; the proximo-distal segment is read from the truncation fraction of the wild-type length via a 1/3-2/3 trisection, and the Saunders / Summerbell comparison is to an ordinal stage -> segment summary (+/- 1 stage between studies), not to digitised truncation data",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2D model is a reduced phenomenological coupling: the production rates s_F, s_S, feedback gain g_S and half-saturations K_S, K_FS, K_g are tuned so that wild-type FGF ~ 1 and L_final ~ 660 um, not taken from any paper; the developmental clock is compressed (12 h of model time spans HH18 -> HH28, ~5x faster than in ovo) while keeping tau_relax << tau_growth",
        "transfer_boundary: The paddle geometry is prescribed (fixed AP width 500 um, elliptical 150 um cap); the AER is the distal-facing rim row and the ZPA is the posterior-margin mesenchyme within 120 um of the rim by construction, so their positions are inputs, not emergent; new lattice rows appear with zero concentration (no proliferation field)",
        "transfer_boundary: The specimen is a whole-egg 72 h embryo photograph whose radial area-vasculosa profile is used as a proxy gradient; no limb bud image or Shh / Fgf in situ is compared with the 2D output" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Gallus" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/469bf3c/1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py; output: docs/media/french_flag_morphogen_comparison.png; organism: Chick embryo (Gallus gallus domesticus) wing bud & embryonic blastoderm; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/469bf3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 2318acced0a431554f620954ae7793615d43475a0b43ba5e6a33b913a35b9af8; artifact_sha256: 8c085a38c660bc8306e75d1e8f570fd260932d2b0fcbe3d7a50ff07c7f1fcedd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/french_flag_morphogen/french_flag_morphogen_reference.json=deae09091fa98a1b..., datasets/french_flag_morphogen/french_flag_specimen.jpg=7163e90c56e1316e..., datasets/french_flag_morphogen/limb_bud_2d_aer_zpa_reference.json=c34af92f3747bb64..., datasets/french_flag_morphogen/scout_manifest.json=d3bd7cc1c62dd2cb...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-french-flag-morphogen-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Wolpert (1969): positional information read from a monotone morphogen gradient against thresholds gives size-invariant French-Flag proportions under linear source-sink diffusion; Crick (1970): synthesis-diffusion-degradation gives lambda = sqrt(D/k) and the positional-error law sigma_x = sigma_c / |dc/dx| | Tickle, Summerbell & Wolpert (1975) and Tickle (1981): a posterior ZPA specifies wing digits 2-3-4; an anterior graft gives the mirror duplication 4-3-2-2-3-4, and the digit specified next to a weaker graft advances 2 -> 3 -> 4 with polarizing-cell number; Riddle et al. (1993): Shh mediates ZPA activity | Saunders (1948) and Summerbell (1974): AER removal arrests outgrowth and truncates the limb at a level that is progressively more distal the later the excision; Summerbell, Lewis & Wolpert (1973): proximo-distal values are laid down by time spent in the distal progress zone | Laufer et al. (1994) and Niswander et al. (1994): Shh in the ZPA and Fgf4 in the posterior AER maintain each other (Shh lost after AER removal, rescued by FGF4 bead; ectopic anterior Fgf4 after a ZPA graft); Crossley et al. (1996): Fgf8 is expressed along the whole ridge | Ben-Zvi & Barkai (2010): an expander produced where morphogen is low scales the decay length with domain size; reconstructed_in_script: 1D linear source-sink and SDD solvers (analytic + explicit PDE, RMSE 7.6e-6), 6-stage growth-scaling sweep with expansion-repression, 5-regime 1D ZPA suite (wild type, full / attenuated / weak anterior graft, ablation) read by a morphogen-valley digit rule, 400-trial Monte Carlo positional-error test, radial segmentation of the vendored 72 h embryo photograph | Pass 3: explicit 2D finite-difference solver for FGF and Shh on a growing paddle mask (dx = 12.5 um) with zero-flux boundaries, Michaelis-form Shh<->FGF feedback, AER-driven distal apposition growth, graft dose series, AER excision at five stages, ZPA ablation, a rectangle verification against the 1D cosh steady state, 8 new reference-anchored measurements and 7 new Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: The 2D model is a reduced phenomenological coupling: the production rates s_F, s_S, feedback gain g_S and half-saturations K_S, K_FS, K_g are tuned so that wild-type FGF ~ 1 and L_final ~ 660 um, not taken from any paper; the developmental clock is compressed (12 h of model time spans HH18 -> HH28, ~5x faster than in ovo) while keeping tau_relax << tau_growth | The paddle geometry is prescribed (fixed AP width 500 um, elliptical 150 um cap); the AER is the distal-facing rim row and the ZPA is the posterior-margin mesenchyme within 120 um of the rim by construction, so their positions are inputs, not emergent; new lattice rows appear with zero concentration (no proliferation field) | Digit identity is read from the instantaneous distal Shh concentration against the Pass 2 thresholds normalised to the wild-type peak; the proximo-distal segment is read from the truncation fraction of the wild-type length via a 1/3-2/3 trisection, and the Saunders / Summerbell comparison is to an ordinal stage -> segment summary (+/- 1 stage between studies), not to digitised truncation data | The specimen is a whole-egg 72 h embryo photograph whose radial area-vasculosa profile is used as a proxy gradient; no limb bud image or Shh / Fgf in situ is compared with the 2D output; does_not_claim: Digit condensation or Turing-type periodicity, temporal integration of Shh exposure (Harfe 2004), a dorsoventral axis or 3D geometry, measured growth curves of the chick wing bud, quantitative Fgf4 / Shh expression levels, or a mechanistic derivation of AER and ZPA position]; other sources: A quantitative analysis of the effect of excision of the AER from the chick limb-bud <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/4463222/>" ;
