<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolpert (1969) French Flag positional information, Tickle-Wolpert (1975) chick limb ZPA digit duplication, Ben-Zvi-Barkai (2010) scaling & 2D AER-FGF / ZPA-Shh limb bud paddle — Morphological realism / specimen match: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-locked 72 h embryo photograph is still segmented and overlaid with concentric French-Flag rings (Panels E-F, L844-929; r = 0.9963), and the digit-count comparisons with Tickle's wings remain exact in 1D and now in 2D (Panels C, G, H). The new 2D output is a recognisable limb bud paddle with a posterior-distal Shh domain and a ridge-wide FGF field, and the GIF shows wild type, a duplicated bud and an AER-excised stump side by side. Deductions, now priced in more strictly than in v2: the specimen is a whole-egg photo whose area vasculosa is a proxy, not a morphogen gradient, and it is not a limb bud, so nothing in Panels G-I is compared with a real wing bud image, an Shh / Fgf in situ or Saunders' or Summerbell's own figures (-8); the paddle outline is a prescribed mask with fixed AP width, so its shape cannot be credited as a morphological match (-4); the anterior-graft bud grows longer (687 um, HH29) rather than broader, unlike duplicated wings (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
